Subject: reader: keep the gpu_busy_percent reader, add the VRAM counters, read each with one pread of a file kept open
Why: hex-gpu reads AMD GPUs through amdgpu's sysfs counters (docs/design/gpu-telemetry.md G2): all-smi's gpu_busy_percent read is the one place it reads an amdgpu counter directly; the rest of the file drives libamdgpu_top's ioctls and libdrm, which Hex does not take. Each counter is now read with one pread at offset 0 of a file opened once, into a stack buffer, parsed in place: no path joined, no file opened, no String built per sample. A percent past 100 is refused as malformed rather than clamped (CLAUDE.md §3); EPERM, amdgpu's answer for a runtime-suspended GPU, reads as asleep; ENODEV, kernfs's answer once the device is removed, reads as gone; mem_info_vram_used and mem_info_vram_total join it, read the same way.

